webwg for Debian
================

The webwg service starts on install and listens on 127.0.0.1:9999. Put a
reverse proxy with TLS in front of it, since the page where devices ask to
join only works over HTTPS.

It runs as the webwg user holding only CAP_NET_ADMIN, which is enough to
manage WireGuard interfaces, and keeps its database in /var/lib/webwg.

Create the first admin user:

    sudo -u webwg webwg-server --dblogin-add-user admin 'password'

Settings in /etc/webwg/webwg.ini override the defaults shipped in
/usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/webwg/webwg.ini. That file is readable only
by root and the webwg group, since it can hold the GitLab client secret.
